          "id": "the_cohort_row_rule_admits_exactly_the_snapshots_cohorts",
          "description": "125 of the 164 candidates survive `stmyFraction > 0`, and every one of them has an emissionrate row -- so the two suppression mechanisms agree here, which is the fact that distinguishes this slice from process-evap-leaks, where the rate table's absence takes 125 down to 64. `cohortSurvivorCount` counts the cohorts the output carries, so its 125 says both at once; the separate rate-matched count that once stood beside it is gone from the model. n_outputCohort is checked against this, not the other way round.\n\nTHE COHORT GRID IS DAY-FREE, and that is a claim and not an omission. `cohort_rows` is n_agecategory x n_runspecsourcefueltype and stays 164 whichever day types the run selects; the day enters one level down, at `cohDay_*`. So the 250 output rows are 125 cohorts x 2 days and not 250 cohorts, and this count staying at 125 while the output doubles is what says the factorisation is the right one. This snapshot's `emissionrate` carries 69,688 rows against `mixed-onroad`'s 69,200 -- the extra ones are polProcessID 9190, extended idle, which J27 discards on road type -- and the surviving count is unmoved by them.",
