          "id": "the_activity_chain_reproduces_the_worked_examples",
          "description": "docs/expand-day.md §6.1 and §6.2, at the stages a wrong factor shows up at, and at BOTH day types wherever the stage has a day.\n\ntravelFraction is day-INDEPENDENT and is asserted once: [21, 40] normalised over the whole HPMS group is 1.609175e-03; over source type 21 alone it is 4.10e-03 and every row is 2.55x high. Its two ordinals are in the day-2 block and its values are `mixed-onroad`'s unchanged, which is the control on the re-addressing -- a stage with no day cannot move when the day set does.\n\naverageSpeed is the ARITHMETIC mean and it HAS a day: 67.0416879 at hourDayID 72 and 56.3611908 at hourDayID 75, against the reference `averagespeed` table's own 6.70417e+01 and 5.63612e+01. The harmonic means are 51.62 and 40.79, and S8 divides by the result. The weekend figure is one of the three docs/esm-conventions.md §42.4 records as DELETED when the corpus was corrected; it is restored here against the same reference column it was read from.\n\n`act_sho` is asserted at three ages on each day -- the snapshot's own `sho` table, to its stored digits. The day-2 and day-5 values at the same age differ by a factor of 10.51 and that factor is the whole day axis of S6-S9 in one number: 27.33 / 260.057 = 0.105093 = (0.237635 / 0.762365) x (0.0184304 / 0.0459565) x (56.3611908 / 67.0416879), i.e. dayVMTFraction x hourVMTFraction x 1/averageSpeed and nothing else. Omitting weeksPerMonth multiplies all six by 4.428571.",
