                "runspecmonth_rows": 1
              },
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-12
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_day_axis_is_exercised_at_both_of_its_values",
          "description": "THE REASON THIS FIXTURE EXISTS. docs/esm-conventions.md §42.5: the `<day key=>` correction left every two-valued day factor in this repository exercised at exactly ONE value -- noOfRealDays always 5, hourDayID always 75, dayVMTFraction four rows and not eight -- so a port that hardcoded any of them passed all twelve remaining fixtures. `expand-day` is the one snapshot in the corpus that still carries both day types, and this test is where that is spent.\n\nFOUR DAY-KEYED QUANTITIES, EACH AT BOTH VALUES, in the order the chain reaches them:\n\n  1. the key      day_hourDayID {72, 75} -- LOOKED UP from (dayID, hourID) through `hourday`, never composed as hourID x 10 + dayID\n  2. the layout   act_hourDayID at the first row of each block of `activity_rows`\n  3. the output   out_dayID and outHourDayID at ordinals 1, 125, 126 and 250 of `output_rows`\n  4. S16's divisor  outNoOfRealDays {2, 5} on both output blocks\n\nEVERY ONE IS A COMPUTED VARIABLE AND NONE IS AN INGESTED COLUMN, which is forced rather than chosen: an assertion naming a `kind: data` parameter -- `rsd_dayID`, `dow_dayID`, `dow_noOfRealDays`, and every other column this document ingests -- fails at evaluation with `array state '...' has no cells in var_map` (finding F43). So `dayofanyweek.noOfRealDays` cannot be pinned where it is READ; it is pinned at `outNoOfRealDays`, where it is USED, which is the stronger of the two claims anyway -- a divisor that arrives correctly and is then not applied fails the second and not the first.\n\nWHAT EACH WOULD CATCH, stated as the failure and not as the property, because a claim nobody can falsify is decoration:\n\n  * noOfRealDays hardcoded to 5, or the divisor dropped: the asserted day-2 `outNoOfRealDays` cells go red here, and the four day-2 emissionQuant cells of `the_four_worked_examples_reach_MOVESOutput` go red at exactly 2.5x. Measured: the day-2 rows land 2.5x high with the divisor dropped and 2.5x high with it pinned at 5 -- the same wrong answer twice, which is why the OUTPUT assertions and these structural ones are both needed.\n  * the day index dropped from `hourday`, so both blocks read hourDayID 75: `day_hourDayID[1]`, `act_hourDayID[1]` and `outHourDayID[1]` go red, and behind them `act_sho`, `dc_W` and every `cohDay_*` day-2 cell, because 72 and 75 are what `sho` and `avgspeeddistribution` are keyed on.\n  * dayVMTFraction or hourVMTFraction taken from whichever row matches first rather than by day: the two shares are 0.237635/0.762365 and 0.0184304/0.0459565, so a first-match join reads the day-2 value into both blocks and `act_sho`'s day-5 rows fall by 3.2x and 2.5x. The shares themselves are not asserted here (their `act_*` variables are gone); such a join is caught downstream, by the worked examples' day-5 emissionQuant cells.\n  * the day labels and divisors on the output: ordinals 1, 125, 126 and 250 are day 2, 2, 5, 5. `output_rows` is now (cohort, day) with the day INNERMOST (odd ordinals day 2, even day 5), and those four ordinals carry the same days under that layout as under the day-outermost one these assertions were written against -- so they check the labels and divisors but NOT the layout. The layout is pinned by `the_four_worked_examples_reach_MOVESOutput`, which finds each cohort at the pair of rows it now occupies. The layout was MEASURED and not assumed (§42.3).\n\nThe values are exact stored decimals in the snapshot's own tables, so the gate is the document's own 1e-9 rather than the reference's six-figure storage: nothing here is computed, everything is read and carried, and a carried number that has drifted at 1e-9 has been through an arithmetic step it should not have been through.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "tolerance": {
            "rel": 1e-09
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.day_hourDayID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 72.0,
              "coords": {
                "runspecday_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
